Engineering Summary

The solution implements a production-style URL Shortener service using Spring Boot and MySQL.

The application supports URL shortening, redirection, analytics tracking, and agentic workflow orchestration.

The SDLC lifecycle is represented through specialized agents that perform requirement analysis, design, implementation, testing, documentation, and release readiness activities.

Governance controls have been implemented through approval checkpoints, retry handling, and audit logging.

The solution also demonstrates greenfield development, brownfield enhancement analysis, and ambiguous requirement handling.

The architecture is modular, extensible, testable, and aligned with controlled autonomy principles where agents execute tasks while humans retain governance and approval authority.